= Practice Questions (Exam Pattern)

Ten questions in the CUET UG style — everyday mechanisms, one observation puzzle, and two judgement calls. Every answer must carry its mechanism. Each correct answer earns $+5$; each incorrect one costs $-1$.

#mcq(1, [We see lightning before we hear thunder because:], (
  [thunder takes time to grow loud], [light travels much faster than sound], [clouds absorb sound waves], [lightning happens first in time],
))

#mcq(2, [Ice floats on water because:], (
  [ice is heavier than water], [ice is less dense than water], [water pushes ice up with heat], [ice contains trapped air only],
))

#mcq(3, [Food cooks faster in a pressure cooker because:], (
  [the sealed lid keeps all flavours inside], [higher pressure raises the boiling point of water above 100°C], [the cooker heats food from all sides], [steam is hotter than any flame],
))

#mcq(4, [Sweating cools the body because:], (
  [sweat is colder than blood], [evaporation of sweat carries heat away from the skin], [sweat blocks sunlight], [sweat reflects heat like a mirror],
))

#mcq(5, [A message claims: "One pill instantly cures all fevers with no side effects." The MOST reasonable response is to:], (
  [forward it — herbal means safe], [reject it until real evidence and a mechanism are shown], [try one dose to test it personally], [believe it, since it sounds scientific],
))

#mcq(6, [A metal spoon left in hot soup feels hot at the handle because heat travels by:], (
  [conduction along the metal], [convection in the spoon], [radiation from the bowl], [evaporation of the soup],
))

#mcq(7, [Leaves look green because chlorophyll:], (
  [produces green light], [absorbs green light strongly], [reflects green light while absorbing red and blue], [stores sunlight as green pigment],
))

#mcq(8, [A burning candle covered by an inverted glass goes out because the flame:], (
  [is crushed by the glass], [runs out of oxygen inside the glass], [melts the wax too fast], [gets too cold under glass],
))

#mcq(9, [Spreading salt on icy roads melts the ice because salt:], (
  [heats the road surface], [lowers the freezing point of water], [absorbs the ice chemically], [blocks cold air from below],
))

#mcq(10, [A city records that mosquito-disease cases rise every year in the weeks after heavy rains. The BEST-supported conclusion is that:], (
  [rain directly causes the diseases], [standing water after rains provides mosquito breeding sites, raising cases], [mosquitoes become stronger in rainy weeks], [hospitals report more carefully after rains],
))

= Detailed Solutions

Each solution shows the working, not just the verdict — cover the answer line, attempt the reasoning, then compare.

#solution(1, [The flash and the crack are born together; light outruns sound by a huge margin, so the flash wins the race to your eyes. "Happens first in time" is the tempting nonsense option.], answer: [B])

#solution(2, [Water expands as it freezes, so ice is LESS dense than liquid water and floats. Option A is the exact reverse; trapped air is not the cause.], answer: [B])

#solution(3, [Pressure raises water's boiling point above 100°C, so the food sits in hotter water and cooks faster. "Keeps flavours in" may be true of lids generally — but it is not the cooking-speed mechanism.], answer: [B])

#solution(4, [Turning liquid sweat into vapour takes energy, and that energy is drawn as heat from your skin — evaporation is the cooling engine.], answer: [B])

#solution(5, [Run the checklist: no evidence, no mechanism, three alarm words ("instantly", "all fevers", "no side effects"). The reasonable response demands evidence first. Testing it personally on a real fever is exactly what the claim wants you to do.], answer: [B])

#solution(6, [Metal is a conductor: heat flows atom to atom along the spoon from the hot end to the handle. The soup stays put — nothing convects inside solid metal.], answer: [A])

#solution(7, [Chlorophyll absorbs red and blue wavelengths for photosynthesis and bounces green back to your eyes — we see the reflected colour, not an emitted one.], answer: [C])

#solution(8, [The glass traps a fixed pocket of air; the flame consumes its oxygen, and once oxygen runs short, combustion stops. Nothing "crushes" or "freezes" the flame.], answer: [B])

#solution(9, [Salt dissolves into the surface water and lowers its freezing point, so ice melts even when the road stays below 0°C — no heating involved.], answer: [B])

#solution(10, [Mechanism-backed conclusion: rains leave standing water — the classic breeding site — so mosquito numbers, and the diseases they carry, rise in the following weeks. Option A names a cause with no mechanism; option D invents a reporting story absent from the data.], answer: [B])

